igned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $(-1-\\frac{10\\sqrt{2}}{3},0)$ and $(-1+\\frac{10\\sqrt{2}}{3},0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401573 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401573 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401573 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401573 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401577 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401573 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401578 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401573 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401573 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401573 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186401576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401573 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d58b31e7-b6c4-5d90-9a58-b8914d59f384" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401574 #edb/ref 1080 "There is no $x$-intercept" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401574 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401574 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0e455adf-7973-5ee4-bb3c-0bd83316580a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401575 #edb/ref 1080 "(1\\pm \\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2},0)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401575 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401575 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d3568acd-90d7-5e24-95a2-7dddb6de4815" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401576 #edb/ref 1080 "(-1\\pm \\frac{10\\sqrt{2}}{3},0)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401576 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401576 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d33bd951-6cf6-508d-8421-15a11016a317" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401577 #edb/ref 1080 "(\\pm \\sqrt{5},0)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401577 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401577 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "829db562-f4d5-5e31-b45c-b397742cb7e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401578 #edb/ref 1080 "(1\\pm \\frac{10\\sqrt{2}}{3},0)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401578 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401578 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a69ed72a-53dd-5923-8c05-9efa0f54638b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403349 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403349 #edb/ref 1069 "q-70185" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403349 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403349 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the points where the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-8x-4y=8$ intercepts the $y$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403349 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bb24f0ce-8ec6-592f-8577-163f3821ff7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403349 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the $y$-intercepts, we need to substitute $x=0$ in the equation of the ellipse and try to solve the resulting equation for $y.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-8x-4y & =8 \\\\ 4\\cdot {0}^{2}+{y}^{2}-8\\cdot 0-4y & =8 \\\\ {y}^{2}-4y & =8 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-4 & =8 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =8+4 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =12 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ x & =2\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,2-2\\sqrt{3})$ and $(0,2+2\\sqrt{3}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403350 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403350 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403350 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403350 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403350 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403350 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403350 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403350 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186403351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403350 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "95684ce7-0099-5fec-8c6e-29f3ec84dc36